  "scope": "Two independent author builds reproduce the complete Ruby gem. Offline installation follows author removal; unchanged callers replay after moving the installed tree, giving two executions per selection. The full API checks all nineteen primitive fields, per-site constructors and normalization, repeated fields, active variants, aliases, mixed Fin guards, exact rejection paths, caller snapshots and recovery. Primitive-base nominal Ruby acceptance covers the tested acyclic records, variants, aliases, mixed Fin guards and constructor-free results over Unit, Bool, UInt8, UInt16, UInt32, UInt64, Int8, Int16, Int32, Int64, Nat, Int, Float32, Float, String, ByteArray, Char, USize and ISize. Both author routes and full/result-only APIs reproduce complete gems from two author roots, install offline after author removal and replay after moving the installed tree on MRI Ruby 3.3.12, Linux x64/glibc 2.36 and 64-bit machine words. Original gems, complete package identities, execution/control records, the preserved failed launch and selected sources are retained; external toolchain binaries are not. Other hosts require their own primitive-base nominal acceptance. Refined callbacks, owned, recursive, dependent and broader generic Subtypes remain separate work. Constructor/source entry counts and memory are unmeasured. These local runs do not establish hosted release-floor acceptance; archived absolute paths describe the original machine and are not CI prerequisites.",
